{
  "program": "CBACT04C",
  "caseId": "case19",
  "description": "THE PARM IS CHARACTER DATA, NOT A DATE. app/jcl/INTCALC.jcl:22 is EXEC PGM=CBACT04C,PARM='2022071800' and the LINKAGE SECTION at :176-178 receives it as PARM-LENGTH PIC S9(04) COMP followed by PARM-DATE PIC X(10) - an alphanumeric item. The only thing the program does with it is STRING it into TRAN-ID at :476-480, so it is never parsed, never validated and never compared against a calendar. This case proves that by supplying 2022071899, whose trailing 99 is not an hour: every identifier becomes 2022071899000001 and the run is otherwise byte-identical to case02 - same account row from acctdata.txt, same balance, same 12.50 rate under the 'DEFAULT' group, same 10.41. A translation that parsed the PARM as a date would reject this value or reformat it, and either way this case would fail while case02 passed - which is exactly the divergence it exists to catch.",
